## 2. System context (what exists vs what we build)

**Already exists (do NOT build; integrate via clients):**
- ASR, noise-cancellation, turn-detection, TTS, telephony/CPaaS (Fonada voice layer).
- Internal **KB** holding hashed flows, exposed via an HTTP endpoint.
- A **tool section** (LMS / payment / etc.) exposed via an HTTP endpoint.

**We build (this repo): the engine between them.**
A stateless-per-request FastAPI service exposing `POST /turn`: transcript in → gated reply + executed actions + persisted state out. State lives in Upstash, keyed by call/borrower.

```
[ASR] → transcript ─▶  ┌──────────────── THIS ENGINE ────────────────┐  ─▶ reply text → [TTS]
                       │ safety → retrieve → command-gen(LLM) →       │
                       │ tracker/memory → priority → executor →       │
                       │ tools(governed) → NLG → COMPLIANCE GATE      │
                       └──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

