| Live state / memory | **Upstash Redis** (REST client `upstash-redis` or `httpx`) | hot state + borrower record cache + event log |
| Durable audit store | `DECISION NEEDED:` default **Postgres** (audit retention) | Upstash Redis is hot-first; RBI retention needs durable store. Default: append events to Redis + periodic export to Postgres. |
| Flows/KB | **external endpoint** (your internal KB) via `KBClient` | retrieval = POST transcript → candidate flows |
| Tools | **external endpoint** (your tool section) via `ToolClient` | read + write tools; write tools idempotent |
| HTTP | `httpx` (async) | all external calls async with timeouts |
| Tests | `pytest`, `pytest-asyncio` | golden, unit, compliance suites |
| Tracing | OpenTelemetry (optional P1, required P2) | per-turn span with the decision chain |
| Lint/format | `ruff` + `black` + `mypy` | enforced in CI |

**Latency budget (text path, engine only):** target p95 ≤ 700 ms with ≤ 1 LLM call/turn. Read tools may run inside the turn; slow/external write tools should be async where possible.

